# Cursor Rules - Xenity Engine
# Refer to AGENT.md for full context.

1. Automatically check `knowledge_base/CURRENT_STATUS.md` first to know the live active phase and milestones. Never guess or ask "where are we currently?".
2. All graphics algorithms must be backed by official repositories and academic papers listed in `knowledge_base/references/01_source_provenance_and_citations.md` (CryEngine, OpenLara, Urho3D, etc.).
3. Whenever creating design plans, research, or graphics proposals, automatically save them as markdown files in `knowledge_base/<category>/` using `knowledge_base/templates/ai_document_template.md` and update `CURRENT_STATUS.md`.
4. Target Platforms: Linux (native CMake/ELF), Windows, PS3 (256MB VRAM limit), Xbox 360, PS Vita, PSP (fixed-function only).
5. Language Standards: Engine Core is C++17, Editor is Rust 2024 (eframe/wgpu on Vulkan for Linux).
6. ALWAYS execute the editor with `cargo run --release --manifest-path xenity-editor/Cargo.toml`. Never run in debug mode.
7. Always keep the codebase cross-platform and memory-constrained.
